{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788566",
      "title": "Using Signal Inputs",
      "lectureOrder": 33,
      "videoOrder": 29,
      "sourceHash": "a14793e50b28b6d68f415300019927c717da16b144c4ef07dcdce03180664248",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "So this is how you can accept inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 5.61,
          "en": "in your components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.61,
          "end": 10.284,
          "en": "So properties or custom attributes, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.284,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "you can set on your own components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "to pass data into them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 18.3,
          "en": "Now, earlier in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 23.28,
          "en": "I showed you an alternative way of managing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.28,
          "end": 26.508,
          "en": "So of managing data that may change over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.508,
          "end": 30.633,
          "en": "and where those changes should then be reflected in the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.47,
          "end": 34.65,
          "en": "And that alternative modern approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.65,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "offered by Angular works with so-called signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 43.89,
          "en": "Now it turns out that you can also use signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.89,
          "end": 45.93,
          "en": "for accepting inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.93,
          "end": 49.77,
          "en": "instead of using this @Input decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.77,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "And therefore, I also want to introduce you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "to how you would accept inputs with signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.95,
          "en": "so that you do know about both approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 61.56,
          "en": "And of course, you'll then also see both approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.56,
          "end": 64.02,
          "en": "in action throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.02,
          "end": 66.51,
          "en": "Now to accept an Input as a signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.51,
          "end": 70.41,
          "en": "you start by importing the input function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.41,
          "end": 72.57,
          "en": "from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.57,
          "end": 74.596,
          "en": "input with a lowercase I.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.596,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "That's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.71000000000001,
          "en": "With an uppercase, it's that decorator;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.71000000000001,
          "end": 82.473,
          "en": "with a lowercase, it's a special function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.91,
          "end": 85.618,
          "en": "Now with that imported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.618,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "you can then replace these inputs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 91.957,
          "en": "by still adding properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.957,
          "end": 93.53999999999999,
          "en": "with the intended names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.53999999999999,
          "end": 96.27000000000001,
          "en": "like avatar as we did it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 99.15,
          "en": "But instead of adding a decorator in front of them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.15,
          "end": 101.03999999999999,
          "en": "you now assign a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.03999999999999,
          "end": 105,
          "en": "and initial value to these properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "And that value is the result of calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 109.473,
          "en": "that input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.4,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "That internally tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 114.99000000000001,
          "en": "that this avatar property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "should be an input to this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 120.224,
          "en": "so that it should be set as an attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.224,
          "end": 122.613,
          "en": "when that component is used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 127.83,
          "en": "Now that's not all you typically do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "with that input function though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 133.71,
          "en": "Instead, you can also assign a default value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.71,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "which will be assumed if no input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 137.91,
          "en": "has been received yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 140.253,
          "en": "which could, for example, be an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.69,
          "end": 145.82999999999998,
          "en": "Alternatively, you can also not pass an initial value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.82999999999998,
          "end": 149.286,
          "en": "and therefore the initial value would be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.286,
          "end": 152.91,
          "en": "But you can tell TypeScript in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.91,
          "end": 156.87,
          "en": "and therefore implicitly of course also Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.87,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "that eventually a value of a different type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 161.31,
          "en": "will be received.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.31,
          "end": 165.32999999999998,
          "en": "For example, here, that eventually a string will be received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.32999999999998,
          "end": 169.70600000000002,
          "en": "by adding angle brackets after this input function name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.70600000000002,
          "end": 171.873,
          "en": "but before the parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.71,
          "end": 174.6,
          "en": "And between those angle brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.6,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "you can set the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 180.783,
          "en": "that will eventually be by that input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.4,
          "end": 185.13,
          "en": "Now this angle bracket syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.13,
          "end": 189.27,
          "en": "is not some Angular specific syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 191.382,
          "en": "instead that's a TypeScript thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.382,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "It's a so-called generic type we're dealing with here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 200.49,
          "en": "input, the input function is a generic function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.49,
          "end": 203.64,
          "en": "set up to be generic by the Angular team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.64,
          "end": 205.92000000000002,
          "en": "which in the end means it's a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.92000000000002,
          "end": 210.92000000000002,
          "en": "that's able to work with a broad variety of value types,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.99,
          "end": 215.94,
          "en": "a broad variety of input value types in this case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.94,
          "end": 218.79,
          "en": "And with that angle bracket syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.79,
          "end": 221.237,
          "en": "we simply tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.237,
          "end": 226.14,
          "en": "which kind of value will eventually be received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.14,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "by that input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 230.57999999999998,
          "en": "And that then can help us further down the road",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.57999999999998,
          "end": 232.92000000000002,
          "en": "when we work with that input value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.92000000000002,
          "end": 236.25,
          "en": "So when we work with this avatar property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 239.25,
          "en": "because TypeScript then will know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 241.5,
          "en": "that this avatar property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.5,
          "end": 244.65,
          "en": "will hold a signal in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.65,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "since input, this input function produces a signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 250.26,
          "en": "So a data container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 250.26,
          "end": 252.49,
          "en": "but inside of that data container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 253.534,
          "end": 256.05,
          "en": "will eventually have a string value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.05,
          "end": 258.702,
          "en": "That's the idea behind this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.702,
          "end": 261.24,
          "en": "And you'll see it from time to time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 261.24,
          "end": 263.4,
          "en": "when working with TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.4,
          "end": 266.253,
          "en": "not just in Angular projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 270.756,
          "en": "You can also mark an input as required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 270.756,
          "end": 274.40999999999997,
          "en": "by calling input.required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "So a modified version of that function, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 280.62,
          "en": "That's the equivalent of setting required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 280.62,
          "end": 282.723,
          "en": "with the @Input decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 283.65,
          "end": 285.18,
          "en": "Now when using required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 285.18,
          "end": 288.33,
          "en": "you can't pass an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 288.33,
          "end": 290.19,
          "en": "As you see, I'm getting an arrow here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.19,
          "end": 292.44,
          "en": "Because if this input is required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 292.44,
          "end": 295.5,
          "en": "you are telling Angular that it will be set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.5,
          "end": 298.40999999999997,
          "en": "So an initial value of course makes no sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 298.40999999999997,
          "end": 301.53,
          "en": "because there will be a value set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 301.53,
          "end": 304.44,
          "en": "from outside of this component anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.44,
          "end": 305.273,
          "en": "So in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 305.273,
          "end": 307.08,
          "en": "you should just tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.08,
          "end": 310.02,
          "en": "which kind of value will be set here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.02,
          "end": 312.603,
          "en": "by using this angle bracket syntax again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.07,
          "end": 315.51,
          "en": "And then we could do the same thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 315.51,
          "end": 317.16,
          "en": "with the name input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 317.16,
          "end": 319.77,
          "en": "With name = input.required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 319.77,
          "end": 322.383,
          "en": "which will also be a string like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 324.66,
          "end": 327.09,
          "en": "And that's simply an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 327.09,
          "end": 328.53,
          "en": "of accepting inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 328.53,
          "end": 331.173,
          "en": "instead of using this decorator approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 332.22,
          "end": 334.68,
          "en": "Now what's really important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 334.68,
          "end": 338.13,
          "en": "and keep in mind when setting up inputs like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 338.13,
          "end": 340.74,
          "en": "as signal inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 340.74,
          "end": 344.52,
          "en": "is that from outside this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 344.52,
          "end": 347.61,
          "en": "so in this case from inside the app.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 347.61,
          "end": 349.98,
          "en": "you still use them like before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 349.98,
          "end": 354.65999999999997,
          "en": "You still set those inputs with this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 354.65999999999997,
          "end": 356.58,
          "en": "So by setting the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 356.58,
          "end": 358.929,
          "en": "that are marked as inputs as attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 358.929,
          "end": 363.929,
          "en": "you could say, on your custom elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.93,
          "end": 366.3,
          "en": "you can still use data binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 366.3,
          "end": 369.72,
          "en": "property binding to set them to a dynamic value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 369.72,
          "end": 374.52,
          "en": "And that value here also doesn't have to be a signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 374.52,
          "end": 377.43,
          "en": "Indeed, here in my application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 377.43,
          "end": 379.02,
          "en": "in the app.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 379.02,
          "end": 382.41,
          "en": "this user's array is a normal array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 382.41,
          "end": 385.83,
          "en": "It's not wrapped in a signal or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 385.83,
          "end": 389.853,
          "en": "So I'm passing a non signal value as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 389.853,
          "end": 392.43,
          "en": "to this input signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 392.43,
          "end": 395.01,
          "en": "And that's really important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 395.01,
          "end": 397.5,
          "en": "that from outside this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 397.5,
          "end": 400.65,
          "en": "it doesn't matter whether your inputs are set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 400.65,
          "end": 404.463,
          "en": "with that input decorator or this input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 405.36,
          "end": 407.88,
          "en": "Now one advantage we can already see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 407.88,
          "end": 411.24,
          "en": "inside of this function where we are using input though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 411.24,
          "end": 413.64,
          "en": "is that we, for example, no longer need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 413.64,
          "end": 415.11,
          "en": "that exclamation mark",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 415.11,
          "end": 417.873,
          "en": "because we're now no longer setting up a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 417.873,
          "end": 421.2,
          "en": "which technically doesn't have an initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 421.2,
          "end": 423.03,
          "en": "as it was the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 423.03,
          "end": 426.12,
          "en": "But instead now from a technical point of view,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 426.12,
          "end": 428.036,
          "en": "the avatar and name properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 428.036,
          "end": 430.8,
          "en": "do have values assigned to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 430.8,
          "end": 434.76,
          "en": "They do have these input signal objects assigned to them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 434.76,
          "end": 437.04,
          "en": "which then will, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 437.04,
          "end": 439.44,
          "en": "internally hold some other value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 439.44,
          "end": 442.14,
          "en": "since they act as data containers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 442.14,
          "end": 447.14,
          "en": "and those internal values will be the actual input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 447.57,
          "end": 450.51,
          "en": "But that's still one nice thing to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 450.51,
          "end": 451.92,
          "en": "that we no longer need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 451.92,
          "end": 455.82,
          "en": "to convince TypeScript that we will have values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 455.82,
          "end": 459.303,
          "en": "simply because this code here works in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 460.89,
          "end": 464.94,
          "en": "Well, and since avatar and name now are signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 464.94,
          "end": 469.23,
          "en": "we can and should now also use them as signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 469.23,
          "end": 473.22,
          "en": "So in the user component.template file, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 473.22,
          "end": 476.88,
          "en": "you now must execute name as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 476.88,
          "end": 479.82,
          "en": "since that's how you read signal values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 479.82,
          "end": 482.52,
          "en": "and how you get Angular to set up that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 482.52,
          "end": 485.04,
          "en": "behind the scenes subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 485.04,
          "end": 488.733,
          "en": "which does allow it to efficiently update the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 490.5,
          "end": 493.05,
          "en": "And we should also change this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 493.05,
          "end": 495.273,
          "en": "where we calculate the imagePath.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 496.14,
          "end": 498.54,
          "en": "Instead of doing it like this with a getter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 498.54,
          "end": 500.34,
          "en": "we can and should now do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 500.34,
          "end": 502.8,
          "en": "with help of the computed function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 502.8,
          "end": 506.536,
          "en": "So imagePath should be a computed value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 506.536,
          "end": 509.789,
          "en": "which is created with help of that computed function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 509.789,
          "end": 512.91,
          "en": "that's imported from @angular/core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 512.91,
          "end": 516.543,
          "en": "about which you also learned earlier in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 517.71,
          "end": 519.27,
          "en": "And this function, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 519.27,
          "end": 521.46,
          "en": "takes a function as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 521.46,
          "end": 524.55,
          "en": "and that function returns to computed value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 524.55,
          "end": 529.29,
          "en": "But we may and typically will now use a signal in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 529.29,
          "end": 532.02,
          "en": "and we should therefore also call it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 532.02,
          "end": 534.997,
          "en": "because that's always how you read signal values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 534.997,
          "end": 537.39,
          "en": "But since I'm now using computed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 537.39,
          "end": 541.68,
          "en": "Angular will only recompute this imagePath value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 541.68,
          "end": 545.13,
          "en": "whenever this avatar value here changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 545.13,
          "end": 548.1,
          "en": "So it's more efficient than what we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 548.1,
          "end": 549.99,
          "en": "where the getter would be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 549.99,
          "end": 553.863,
          "en": "whenever anything happens to this component, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 555.12,
          "end": 556.8,
          "en": "So that's another adjustment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 556.8,
          "end": 561.123,
          "en": "we should make when using these signal inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 562.17,
          "end": 565.5,
          "en": "Now with that adjustment made imagePath",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 565.5,
          "end": 569.31,
          "en": "is now also a signal, a computed signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 569.31,
          "end": 572.46,
          "en": "or a signal that's created with help of computed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 572.46,
          "end": 575.64,
          "en": "and they offer in the user.component.html file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 575.64,
          "end": 579.57,
          "en": "You now also must execute imagePath as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 579.57,
          "end": 581.52,
          "en": "to read that signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 581.52,
          "end": 584.373,
          "en": "and set up that behind the scenes subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 587.22,
          "end": 589.449,
          "en": "Now what's worth noting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 589.449,
          "end": 592.92,
          "en": "is that these input signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 592.92,
          "end": 596.34,
          "en": "however, are read-only signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 596.34,
          "end": 599.58,
          "en": "which means they in the end only change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 599.58,
          "end": 603.673,
          "en": "or only get new values if the input value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 603.673,
          "end": 608.16,
          "en": "outside of this user component changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 608.16,
          "end": 612.03,
          "en": "So if we would do something here in that app.component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 612.03,
          "end": 616.44,
          "en": "that would change the value set on one of those properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 616.44,
          "end": 618.27,
          "en": "and you will soon see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 618.27,
          "end": 620.88,
          "en": "how you could change a value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 620.88,
          "end": 625.71,
          "en": "then that new value would be received in the user.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 625.71,
          "end": 627.42,
          "en": "but you can't change the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 627.42,
          "end": 630.36,
          "en": "from inside the user.component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 630.36,
          "end": 634.41,
          "en": "So if here inside of this onSelectUser method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 634.41,
          "end": 638.91,
          "en": "I would decide that I wanna change the avatar value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 638.91,
          "end": 640.23,
          "en": "I can't do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 640.23,
          "end": 644.85,
          "en": "If I try to call set on this avatar signal here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 644.85,
          "end": 646.56,
          "en": "you see I'm getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 646.56,
          "end": 649.893,
          "en": "that this does not exist on that input signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 650.76,
          "end": 651.96,
          "en": "And you might recall",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 651.96,
          "end": 653.61,
          "en": "that earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 653.61,
          "end": 656.19,
          "en": "when I introduced you to signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 656.19,
          "end": 658.477,
          "en": "you were able to call the set method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 658.477,
          "end": 661.623,
          "en": "to set a signal to a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 663,
          "end": 666.66,
          "en": "Now it does not work here for these input signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 666.66,
          "end": 670.14,
          "en": "because as I just explained, they are read only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 670.14,
          "end": 673.23,
          "en": "So they can't be changed from inside the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 673.23,
          "end": 675.48,
          "en": "where the inputs are registered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 675.48,
          "end": 678.333,
          "en": "That's just also something to keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 679.47,
          "end": 681.57,
          "en": "Now the obvious question, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 681.57,
          "end": 686.04,
          "en": "therefore is why you would use these inputs here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 686.04,
          "end": 690.33,
          "en": "or why you would use the older decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 690.33,
          "end": 693.494,
          "en": "based approach without signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 693.494,
          "end": 697.11,
          "en": "Well, and the answer is the same as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 697.11,
          "end": 699.57,
          "en": "when I introduced you to signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 699.57,
          "end": 701.64,
          "en": "When working with signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 701.64,
          "end": 704.73,
          "en": "and therefore also when working with signal inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 704.73,
          "end": 707.64,
          "en": "you get this advantage that Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 707.64,
          "end": 710.67,
          "en": "manages these behind the scenes subscriptions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 710.67,
          "end": 715.67,
          "en": "and that Angular is able to update the parts of the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 716.4,
          "end": 718.29,
          "en": "or the values in your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 718.29,
          "end": 723.29,
          "en": "that need updating when such a signal based value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 233,
          "start": 723.42,
          "end": 725.61,
          "en": "So it can be more efficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 234,
          "start": 725.61,
          "end": 729.15,
          "en": "depending on the rest of your application and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 235,
          "start": 729.15,
          "end": 732.15,
          "en": "Now this efficiency might not always matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 236,
          "start": 732.15,
          "end": 734.91,
          "en": "because the other older approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 237,
          "start": 734.91,
          "end": 738.39,
          "en": "without signals is also pretty efficient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 238,
          "start": 738.39,
          "end": 742.38,
          "en": "But even more importantly, this signal feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 239,
          "start": 742.38,
          "end": 745.23,
          "en": "and also these signal inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 240,
          "start": 745.23,
          "end": 749.49,
          "en": "are a relatively new Angular feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 241,
          "start": 749.49,
          "end": 753.15,
          "en": "and therefore many Angular projects out there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 242,
          "start": 753.15,
          "end": 757.74,
          "en": "Actually, the majority of Angular projects out there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 243,
          "start": 757.74,
          "end": 760.23,
          "en": "especially in big companies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 244,
          "start": 760.23,
          "end": 762.715,
          "en": "do not use signals yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 245,
          "start": 762.715,
          "end": 767.37,
          "en": "or not necessarily use them in the entire code base.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 246,
          "start": 767.37,
          "end": 771.33,
          "en": "Therefore, you will definitely encounter lots of code bases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 247,
          "start": 771.33,
          "end": 776.1,
          "en": "and lots of demos and so on that do not use signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 248,
          "start": 776.1,
          "end": 779.97,
          "en": "and that do instead use the Input decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 249,
          "start": 779.97,
          "end": 782.76,
          "en": "for accepting component inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 250,
          "start": 782.76,
          "end": 786.21,
          "en": "which is why you should know about both approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 251,
          "start": 786.21,
          "end": 789.99,
          "en": "and which is actually why I will not continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 252,
          "start": 789.99,
          "end": 791.823,
          "en": "with the signals here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 253,
          "start": 793.11,
          "end": 795,
          "en": "why I will delete that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 254,
          "start": 795,
          "end": 798.393,
          "en": "and why I instead will go back to this decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 255,
          "start": 798.393,
          "end": 801.63,
          "en": "based non signal approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 256,
          "start": 801.63,
          "end": 803.79,
          "en": "which also means that in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 257,
          "start": 803.79,
          "end": 807.903,
          "en": "I no longer call these values as functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 258,
          "start": 809.85,
          "end": 811.2,
          "en": "You could use signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 259,
          "start": 811.2,
          "end": 813.33,
          "en": "you could use the input function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 260,
          "start": 813.33,
          "end": 814.92,
          "en": "But for the reasons mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 261,
          "start": 814.92,
          "end": 817.71,
          "en": "because you'll see plenty of projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 262,
          "start": 817.71,
          "end": 820.35,
          "en": "that do not use those signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 263,
          "start": 820.35,
          "end": 822.48,
          "en": "I'll stick to this code for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 264,
          "start": 822.48,
          "end": 824.64,
          "en": "Of course, throughout this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 265,
          "start": 824.64,
          "end": 827.37,
          "en": "you will see plenty of signal usage though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 266,
          "start": 827.37,
          "end": 829.41,
          "en": "because I want to teach you both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 267,
          "start": 829.41,
          "end": 832.395,
          "en": "And now you do know about both ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 268,
          "start": 832.395,
          "end": 834.69,
          "en": "of accepting component inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 269,
          "start": 834.69,
          "end": 837.963,
          "en": "and both ways are important to know.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
